                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Damn, this one got me in doubt.\n\nI mean, I like it. The minimalist style in everything (story, equipment, even the controls), it's refreshing. Even the unlockables don't really feel like upgrades, given that you have to sacrifice something else on your ships.\n\nBut is too minimalist? I'd have like a bit... more. Not the story - that's perfectly fine. The Emperor is dead and you're doing this out of revenge [spoiler](or are you...)[/spoiler], great, don't need to know more, it's almost straight out of 40k. But I'd have liked to build up my fleet a bit more. Why are my 3 destroyers so much more powerful than the dozens of enemy destroyers I've blown up so far? Why can't I get another frigate? And just 3 fighters, against an entire rebel faction's armada?\n\nI get it, this isn't Homeworld, it's supposed to be a challenge, where you balance aggression and speed versus time and picking your targets. It's still a recommendation, but only heavily discounted.\n\nAlso, I'm absolutely shocked that this developer hasn't done anything since. This game still looks amazing today. Just use it as a base for something more.",
